WEBVTT

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:06.080
My hero is the person who saved my life.

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:11.010
It’s my dream to become as strong as that person,

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:17.030
who I admire, who I dream about, and who I aim to be like.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:22.200
However, our reunion after four years was all too sudden,

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.490
and there’s a lot I’m not sure about.

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:29.990
But something’s about to begin.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:32.760
That’s the feeling I get.

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:38.960
Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha StrikerS<i>
will now begin.</i>

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:37.900
So you remember me.

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:46.130
Not just remember...
I’ve always admired you, Nanoha.

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:47.380
I’m glad.

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:51.090
When I saw your Buster, I was a bit surprised.

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:54.980
I’m sorry for not asking!

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:58.680
It’s okay... I don’t mind.

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:04.280
P.F.C. Lanster, do you know about Nanoha?

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:06.240
Yes, I do.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:10.280
The ace of aces of the Main Office’s Armed Services,

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:16.260
one of the youngest but best air-combat instructors,
Captain Nanoha Takamachi.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.760
Righty-o!

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:21.010
Do they know each other?

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:22.620
From back then, remember?

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:24.010
Four years ago,

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:28.600
when you two came to visit me while I was training...
the airport fire incident.

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:32.020
When we helped with disaster relief?

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:36.530
That’s right.
Subaru was one of the people Nanoha saved.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:40.030
Incidentally, Fate, you saved Subaru’s sister.

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:44.480
Really? I remember saving a girl, but...

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:46.250
That’s the one, that girl!

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:49.040
Now they’re both operatives of the Bureau,

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.120
though they’re in different battalions.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.760
That’s right.

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:16.590
Now that you mention it, they do look alike.

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:26.110
Four years ago, in Mid’s coastal sector,

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:29.840
a fire, started due to a dangerous smuggled item,

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:32.570
engulfed the airport at an overwhelming rate.

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:36.160
Even the Reserve G.A.S. trainees were called in to help with the rescue efforts.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:38.170
It had become a large incident.

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:41.760
Squads 203, 405, please deploy to the east.

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:45.180
Follow your mage leaders and protect those fuel tanks!

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:49.480
Hayate, it’s not going to work.
We don’t have enough mages!

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:53.940
I know, but we don’t have any choice but to hold on until aerial support arrives.

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:54.830
Hang in there!

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:55.680
Okay...

00:04:56.470 --> 00:05:01.640
Being a Special Investigator with the G.A.S.,
Hayate took command of the operation.

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:09.320
Nanoha and I were over visiting Hayate during our vacation,
so we also took part in the rescue efforts.

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:13.160
Aerial mage, this is Main Office 02, please respond.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:16.850
Copy that. Main Office 02, this is Testarossa-Harlaown.

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:19.740
We have a response within Gate 8,

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:22.830
but our operatives cannot advance any further.
Can you look into it for us?

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:24.000
Gate 8...

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.340
Bardiche!

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:26.860
Optimal route calculated.

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:28.370
We will arrive in under two minutes.

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:29.600
I’ll be there shortly.

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:32.830
Keep going south!

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:35.370
Hayate, the guard squad’s commander has arrived!

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:36.840
Sorry for being late.

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:40.860
Not at all. I’m currently stationed with the Ground Armed Service.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:42.990
Captain Hayate Yagami, a Special Investgiator from the Main Office.

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:45.360
I have taken charge of the rescue squad for the time being.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:49.570
Major Genya Nakajima of the Ground Armed Service’s 108th Battalion.

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:51.580
Okay, Major Nakajima.

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:54.080
Can I ask you to take over command of the squadron?

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:57.080
Sure. Are you a mage yourself?

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:58.690
Quite an experienced one.

00:05:58.690 --> 00:06:00.620
I want to help put out the fire from the sky.

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:04.090
Hayate, following your instructions I’ve taken a girl to safety.

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:05.960
Her name’s Subaru Nakajima.

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:10.690
I just dropped her off with the rescue team,
but she said her sister is still inside!

00:06:10.690 --> 00:06:13.170
Roger, I’ll be joining you in the sky soon.

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:14.090
Roger!

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:17.490
Nakajima?

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:18.630
They’re my daughters.

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:22.610
They were supposed to visit me at the base.

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:28.270
Well then, Major Nakajima, please take command of the rest.

00:06:28.270 --> 00:06:29.600
Rein, do your best!

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:32.260
Once you’ve explained everything, I want you to meet up with me!

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:33.140
Gotcha!

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:53.630
I’m from the Bureau!

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:56.330
Over here!

00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:58.060
It’s okay now!

00:06:58.060 --> 00:06:59.790
Defenser Plus

00:07:01.010 --> 00:07:03.740
I’ll take you to safety right away.

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:05.230
Excuse me.

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:06.030
Yes?

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:10.520
You see... a mage girl put up this barrier for us.

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:14.700
And then she said she was going to look for her little sister in that direction!

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:15.680
I understand.

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:19.040
As soon as I get you to safety, I’ll look for her.

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:21.650
Subaru?

00:07:24.070 --> 00:07:26.740
Subaru? Subaru, please answer me!

00:07:27.490 --> 00:07:31.760
Your sister is coming to save you.

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:39.270
You there! Don’t move!

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:40.630
I’m coming to save you now!

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:44.170
Sonic Move

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:55.760
That was dangerous.

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:58.480
Sorry I’m late.

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:00.120
It’s okay now.

00:08:05.470 --> 00:08:07.450
What’s your little sister’s name?

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:09.700
Do you know where she is?

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:13.000
We got separated at the entrance hall.

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:14.960
Her name’s Subaru Nakajima...

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:16.270
...she’s 11 years old.

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:19.440
This is Communications HQ.

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:24.120
Subaru Nakajima, an 11 year old girl,
has already been rescued.

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:26.640
She was saved by Instructor Takamachi.

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:27.550
She is uninjured.

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:31.260
Subaru! Thank goodness!

00:08:31.260 --> 00:08:34.630
Roger. I have her sister here.

00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:35.740
What is your name?

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:40.450
Ginga, Ginga Nakajima, military trainee, 13 years old.

00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:43.200
A trainee, huh?

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:44.990
You’ll be my future colleague.

00:08:44.990 --> 00:08:46.700
I’m honored.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:50.960
The reinforcements?

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:54.920
Eighteen more minutes until Rescue Squad 7 arrives.

00:08:54.920 --> 00:08:59.010
The Air Armed Service will also arrive at the operation within one hour.

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:00.000
Slowpokes!

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.570
How many are in need of rescue?

00:09:01.570 --> 00:09:03.270
Roughly twenty victims.

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:06.730
The mages are working hard... we’ll manage somehow.

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:09.210
Does it look like we can avoid the worst-case scenario?

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:10.370
Yeppers!

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:14.420
Great! That should do for now, my little collaborator friend.

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:17.160
Why don’t you go meet up with your mistress?

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:22.540
It’s okay. I’d like to stay a bit longer to organize information and give instructions.

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:26.370
Oh, I see. Well, that’ll really help.

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:29.880
O ruler of the white snow,

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:31.580
with silver wings,

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:34.970
turn all earth in sight to ice!

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:37.680
Capt. Yagami, the block’s evacuation is complete.

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:38.970
It’s up to you!

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:40.350
Roger!

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:42.970
Come forth, breath of ice.

00:09:43.960 --> 00:09:45.750
<b>Breath of Ice</b>

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:00.980
Incredible!

00:10:00.980 --> 00:10:05.530
So this is the power of an S+ rank mage!

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:08.000
Sorry to get you two involved!

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:11.400
I have trouble controlling this by myself.

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:12.500
Not at all!

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:14.950
We’ll search for the next evacuated block.

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:19.260
Sorry we took so long!

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:23.760
We thank the gentlemen at the scene as well as the aces for the emergency support.

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:26.010
Please leave the rest to us!

00:10:26.010 --> 00:10:31.360
Roger! I’ll continue helping with the rescue effort,
so please give me instructions.

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:36.690
They’ve finally arrived.

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:37.700
Yes!

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:40.000
But we can’t let our guard down yet.

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:42.520
Can I rely on you some more for information management?

00:10:42.520 --> 00:10:43.710
Roger!

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:48.880
Good morning. We’re now going live to the scene.

00:10:49.720 --> 00:10:51.460
I’m reporting live from the scene.

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:53.620
Although the fire has been extinguished,

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:56.270
smoke continues to rise from the area.

00:10:56.270 --> 00:10:58.910
As I speak, operatives from the Time-Space Administrative Bureau

00:10:58.910 --> 00:11:02.220
are conducting investigations into
the dangers as well as the cause of the accident.

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:09.480
Luckily, thanks to the efforts of a group of aerial mages
from the Main Office, there were no casualties.

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:12.710
Just as I thought.

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:19.240
The G.A.S. trainees and the two of you

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:21.990
worked just as hard as Disaster Response
but never got the credit for it

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:25.890
Well, we <i>are</i> on vacation, anyway.

00:11:25.890 --> 00:11:28.020
And the civilians are safe.

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:31.460
You know, Nanoha, Fate,

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:35.460
I want my own unit after all.

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:41.770
For disaster relief like this time, plus crimefighting,
as well as countermeasures for any Lost Logia we find.

00:11:41.770 --> 00:11:45.960
No matter how you look at it, Midchilda’s Bureau units have too many assignments.

00:11:45.960 --> 00:11:49.600
And we shouldn’t just be the rear guard
and do desk work all the time.

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:53.500
Unlike before, I’ve been busy
here and there and have no freedom.

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:55.980
I don’t feel like I’m moving forward at all.

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:58.740
It would be an elite unit.

00:11:58.740 --> 00:12:03.740
And if I succeed,
the powers that be might change just a bit too.

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:11.900
If I did make a unit like that,
Fate, Nanoha, would you cooperate with me?

00:12:14.360 --> 00:12:20.710
Of course if you two don’t want to,
or if you have any reservations, I’d understand, but...

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:23.080
Hayate, what are you being so reserved for?

00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:25.740
Haven’t we known each other since third grade?

00:12:26.590 --> 00:12:32.110
Anyway, if you didn’t invite us to such a fun unit, we would be mad instead.

00:12:32.110 --> 00:12:33.470
Right, Fate?

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:34.170
Right.

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:45.180
Thanks! I appreciate it, Nanoha, Fate!

00:12:58.690 --> 00:13:04.870
And well... because of that, Lt. Colonel Yagami put her efforts towards creating her new unit.

00:13:04.870 --> 00:13:08.990
It took four years, but finally we’ve reached the start of its formation.

00:13:08.990 --> 00:13:10.700
And that’s that.

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:16.190
The squad is called Riot Force 6 of the Time-Space Administrative Bureau’s Antiquities Department!

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:18.020
Registered as a part of the Ground Armed Service,

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:20.940
Riot Force 6’s forward squads will work under G.A.S. mages.

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:24.950
Our job will be investigating antiquities, as well as the collection, management, and protection thereof.

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:28.080
Antiquities. You mean Lost Logia, right?

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:29.270
That’s right.

00:13:29.270 --> 00:13:33.200
But because large-scale investigation
is the job of Riot Forces 1 through 5,

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:35.070
we’ll specialize in tactical work.

00:13:35.070 --> 00:13:36.440
Is that so?

00:13:36.990 --> 00:13:41.520
In short, we’ll primarily be in charge of cases
that specifically have to do with Lost Logia,

00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:43.080
acting as a combined-arms unit.

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:43.630
Okay.

00:13:44.720 --> 00:13:48.170
So, Private First Class Subaru Nakajima...

00:13:48.170 --> 00:13:50.720
And also, Private First Class Teana Lanster...

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:51.720
Yes, ma’am!

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:57.220
I am considering assigning the two of you as forwards in Riot Force 6.

00:13:57.220 --> 00:13:59.820
I know it’ll be hard work to start,

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:04.520
but you’ll gain a lot of experience and have a greater chance of promotion.

00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:06.260
What do you think?

00:14:06.260 --> 00:14:08.320
Um... well...

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:10.060
Subaru would learn magic

00:14:10.060 --> 00:14:12.180
directly from
Instructor Takamachi.

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:13.180
Okay.

00:14:13.180 --> 00:14:15.230
And as Teana is aiming
to be an Enforcer,

00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:16.660
if you have no objections,

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:18.840
I should be able
to give you advice.

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:21.000
Oh no, I don’t mind at all!

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:25.120
Well, in fact, I’m honored! That is...

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:30.220
Um... am I interrupting?

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:32.060
It’s all right.

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:37.020
For the time being, let’s talk about the results of the examination.

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:40.460
Both of you have almost no problems with technique.

00:14:40.460 --> 00:14:45.030
However, your dangerous actions and inability to foresee accidents are too great to allow a pass.

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:50.270
A mage who doesn’t consider her partner’s safety and can’t abide by the exam’s rules

00:14:50.270 --> 00:14:53.050
cannot be trusted to protect people, right?

00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:55.450
That’s right.

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:58.980
That’s why I’m sorry to say that you both failed the exam.

00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:01.560
On the <i>other</i> hand.

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:05.280
Taking your magical powers and abilities into consideration,

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:10.790
it might be more dangerous to keep you two at C rank until the next exam half a year away.

00:15:10.790 --> 00:15:14.230
That is the conclusion that the proctor and I have come to.

00:15:14.230 --> 00:15:15.290
Righty-o!

00:15:15.290 --> 00:15:17.770
So with that said, take this.

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:22.480
It’s a written application as well as a letter of recommendation for a special training course.

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:27.360
Take this with you to a three-day course offered by the Armed Services at the Main Office,

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:29.810
and on the fourth day you’ll be able to retake the final exam.

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:37.070
From next week on, you’ll be under
the care of the strict officers at the Main Office.

00:15:37.070 --> 00:15:39.790
Be sure to learn about safety and rules from them.

00:15:39.790 --> 00:15:43.070
If you do that, then B rank will be easy for you to obtain.

00:15:43.070 --> 00:15:43.860
All right?

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:46.570
Thank you, ma’am!

00:15:46.570 --> 00:15:49.360
Until you pass, you’ll want to concentrate on the exam, right?

00:15:49.360 --> 00:15:53.580
Let’s leave your answers until after you’ve passed the exam.

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:55.350
Sorry and thank you, we are grateful, ma’am!

00:16:00.620 --> 00:16:04.040
Gah! I was nervous about so many things...

00:16:04.040 --> 00:16:05.270
Yeah, I guess.

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:07.600
It’s too bad we didn’t pass, but...

00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:09.250
Well, I guess it can’t be helped.

00:16:09.250 --> 00:16:12.270
Aren’t we lucky, though?
To be able to retake the exam.

00:16:12.270 --> 00:16:13.100
We sure are.

00:16:14.110 --> 00:16:16.860
And well, about the new unit,

00:16:16.860 --> 00:16:18.260
Tia, what do you want to do?

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:20.860
You want to go, don’t you?

00:16:20.860 --> 00:16:23.490
Nanoha is your hero.

00:16:23.490 --> 00:16:26.020
It’d be wonderful if you end up
in the same unit, wouldn’t it?

00:16:26.020 --> 00:16:28.120
Well, I guess so.

00:16:29.120 --> 00:16:31.250
I wonder what I’ll do.

00:16:31.250 --> 00:16:33.880
Normally for a Riot Force in the Antiquities Department,

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:35.850
you’d have to be an expert or have special abilities.

00:16:35.850 --> 00:16:39.220
Otherwise, you can’t get in, right?

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:44.640
With that said, I wonder if I can do that job the way I am now.

00:16:49.970 --> 00:16:51.460
What is it, you’re creeping me out.

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:56.490
“That’s not true at all! You can definitely do it, Tia!”

00:16:56.490 --> 00:16:58.220
Isn’t that what you want me to say?

00:16:59.520 --> 00:17:03.960
What are you talking about? I don’t want you to say that! Don’t be an idiot!

00:17:04.890 --> 00:17:06.530
That really hurt.

00:17:08.350 --> 00:17:09.190
Hey, Tia!

00:17:09.830 --> 00:17:11.700
I already know.

00:17:11.700 --> 00:17:15.080
Whenever you voice your insecurities,

00:17:15.080 --> 00:17:17.330
you’re really thinking the opposite.

00:17:17.330 --> 00:17:21.240
As for Enforcer Fate, you’re seeing a hot rival scene, aren’t you?

00:17:21.240 --> 00:17:26.080
A rival scene? It’s nothing outrageous like that though.

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:30.220
You know, right? It’s my dream to be an Enforcer.

00:17:30.220 --> 00:17:33.670
So if I can accomplish that through studying, I want to do it.

00:17:33.670 --> 00:17:36.240
In that case, let’s do it, Tia!

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:41.740
I’ll learn lots of stuff from Nanoha because I want to become even stronger!

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:44.720
Tia, you’ll gain experience in the new unit

00:17:44.720 --> 00:17:47.570
and achieve your dream through the shortest route.

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:50.380
And let’s not forget...

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:54.900
We aren’t even experts in our fields yet

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:57.320
We should be grateful that they’re accepting us!

00:17:58.120 --> 00:18:00.850
Stop mentioning that!

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:03.250
That irritates me so much!
No matter what we talk about,

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:06.540
no matter where I am,
you’re always fooling around with me!

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:12.240
Well fine then. If this goes well,
it’ll shorten the road to my dreams.

00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:16.240
Though it’s a pain looking after you,
I guess I’ll put up with it.

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:23.380
Wait, what are you laughing about?

00:18:23.380 --> 00:18:26.250
I guess it’s pretty clear those two will sign up.

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:27.510
You’re right.

00:18:27.510 --> 00:18:29.230
Nanoha, you look pretty happy.

00:18:29.230 --> 00:18:31.820
Both of them seem like they’re willing to learn,

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:34.480
so I can take my time and teach them properly.

00:18:35.580 --> 00:18:37.090
That’s for certain!

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:41.080
There were two more forward candidates.
What about them?

00:18:41.080 --> 00:18:44.920
Both of them are from other worlds.
Signum is picking them up now.

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:48.980
Nanoha, Hayate! Sorry for the wait.

00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:50.960
Sorries!

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:54.310
The next time we meet will be at Riot Force 6’s building.

00:18:54.310 --> 00:18:58.570
Your room will be made up super-duper well!

00:18:58.570 --> 00:18:59.560
Great!

00:18:59.560 --> 00:19:00.910
I’m looking forward to it!

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:05.650
Well then, let’s leave it at that and go back.

00:19:05.650 --> 00:19:08.850
I drove in today,
so I can take you to the central region.

00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:10.950
Really? Thanks!

00:19:10.950 --> 00:19:14.960
By the way, Nanoha, are you feeling all right?

00:19:15.700 --> 00:19:18.700
I’m perfectly fine! No problems at all!

00:19:18.700 --> 00:19:20.340
Then that’s okay, but...

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:22.710
You worry too much, Fate.

00:19:22.710 --> 00:19:25.180
You know how tough I am, right?

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:28.350
I know, but I still worry

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:30.100
because I’m your friend.

00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:33.680
I’m really okay, so don’t worry.

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:54.580
Thank you for coming, ma’am!

00:19:54.580 --> 00:19:58.310
I apologize for being in civilian clothing.
I’m Private Erio Mondial.

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:00.790
Sorry I’m late in picking you up.

00:20:00.790 --> 00:20:04.910
First Lieutenant Signum, of the Antiquities Department, Riot Force 6.

00:20:04.910 --> 00:20:06.520
You must have travelled far to get here.

00:20:06.520 --> 00:20:07.880
Not at all!

00:20:07.880 --> 00:20:08.810
What about the other person?

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:11.850
About that, it doesn’t seem she’s come yet.

00:20:11.850 --> 00:20:16.820
So... it’s already past the designated time. She might be lost.

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:19.720
Is it okay if I go look for her?

00:20:19.720 --> 00:20:20.820
Can I count on you?

00:20:20.820 --> 00:20:21.840
Yes, ma’am!

00:20:24.070 --> 00:20:28.320
Ah, so your forward candidates really <i>are</i> those kids.

00:20:28.320 --> 00:20:32.080
They’re both still children, so I’m a bit worried.

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:36.080
But ability-wise, it looks like they’re no problem.

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:41.090
Well they <i>are</i> in my squad,
so if we’re together I can be a bit at ease.

00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:44.090
Miss Lushe! Miss Lushe!

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:47.550
New recruit for the Bureau’s Riot Force 6, Miss Lushe!

00:20:47.550 --> 00:20:50.330
Are you there? Miss Lushe?

00:20:50.330 --> 00:20:54.480
Yes, that’s me! Sorry I’m so late!

00:20:55.810 --> 00:20:57.840
You’re Miss Lushe, right? I’m—

00:21:01.270 --> 00:21:02.510
Sonic Move

00:21:13.460 --> 00:21:14.960
Ow... ow... ouch.

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:17.480
S-Sorry, I screwed up.

00:21:17.480 --> 00:21:21.150
No, thank you very much. You saved me.

00:21:26.040 --> 00:21:27.970
Oh, I’m sorry. I’ll move now.

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:30.390
Um... uh... I’m also sorry!

00:21:34.300 --> 00:21:37.530
Oh! Fried, I’m sorry! Are you okay?

00:21:38.810 --> 00:21:40.760
A baby dragon?

00:21:40.760 --> 00:21:45.040
Excuse me, I’m sorry.
You’re Private Erio Mondial, right?

00:21:45.040 --> 00:21:46.090
Er... yes!

00:21:46.090 --> 00:21:50.900
Nice to meet you, I’m Private Caro Ru Lushe.

00:21:50.900 --> 00:21:55.830
And also, this is Friedrich, my dragon.

00:21:59.990 --> 00:22:03.600
Vita, Zafira, you’ve cornered them.

00:22:03.600 --> 00:22:07.220
Gadgets Type 1. There are three.

00:22:27.730 --> 00:22:28.490
Eisen!

00:22:28.490 --> 00:22:30.480
Flying Swallow

00:22:40.050 --> 00:22:41.540
Have we finished cleaning up?

00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:43.000
Shamal, any remaining?

00:22:44.380 --> 00:22:48.030
No responses or shadows.
We’ve destroyed them all.

00:22:49.500 --> 00:22:53.010
They’re deploying more frequently and in greater numbers.

00:22:53.010 --> 00:22:56.670
Yeah, and their movements are gradually becoming smarter.

00:22:56.670 --> 00:23:00.290
But with this much,
we can still manage with just us.

00:23:00.290 --> 00:23:01.690
That’s right.

00:23:01.690 --> 00:23:05.480
Also, these opponents will give our newbies some problems.

00:23:05.480 --> 00:23:09.190
No choice, we’ll have to manage with just us.

00:23:09.190 --> 00:23:11.380
That’s the reason we have the new unit.

00:23:11.380 --> 00:23:16.800
Hayate’s—no, <i>our</i> new unit.

00:23:18.640 --> 00:23:21.860
Riot Force 6, huh?

00:25:18.100 --> 00:25:19.790
Riot Force 6
has finally been formed!

00:25:19.790 --> 00:25:21.350
All members are assembled.

00:25:21.350 --> 00:25:23.420
I’ll have to work hard enough to not lose to anything!

00:25:23.420 --> 00:25:26.620
And right away, Nanoha’s combat training starts!

00:25:32.260 --> 00:25:33.470
Take off!
